-- title:
--   Two-branch normalisation at the node j=1728: width divides the Fricke exponent
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$ (hypothesis `hker`: $\mathrm{red}\,c = 0$ iff $c$ lies in the maximal ideal). Assume $1728 \in k$ lies in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $1728$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Let $f \neq 0$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $1 \cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series, and assume that $\operatorname{ord}_W f = 0$ for every place $W$ of this field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing the constants whose ideals are principal, $\operatorname{ord}$ being minus the logarithm of its adic valuation) such that, for some $x, y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = 1728$ and $\mathrm{red}\,y = 1728^q$, both $\operatorname{ord}_W(j - x) > 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_W(j(q\tau) - y) > 0$, where $j$ denotes the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` and $j(q\tau)$ that of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`. Then there are $c \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, $c \neq 0$, and $m \in \mathbb Z$ divisible by the width `jWidth (1728 : k)` (which is $2$ unless $1728 = 0$ in $k$, in which case it is $3$), such that the Laurent series of $c \cdot f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red` — the localisation, at the prime of elements with vanishing reduction, of the subring of Laurent series generated by the constants from $A$ together with the two modular generators — and the Laurent series of the Fricke involution `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` applied to $(c \cdot q^m) \cdot f$ lies in that same ring, and the images of both elements under the reduction homomorphism `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red` into $k$-Laurent series are nonzero.
--
--   This is the normalisation step at the supersingular node with invariant $j = 1728$ on the curve $X_0(q)$: a function whose order vanishes along the tube of that node can be scaled so as to be a unit at both branches simultaneously, the scaling exponent picked up by the Fricke involution being divisible by the width of the node (two at $j = 1728$, as in the Deligne–Rapoport model). It is used by [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_int_mul_pow_param_isUnit_of_forall_centred_ofNat1728_ord_eq_zero_of_crossingPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_int_mul_pow_param_isUnit_of_forall_centred_ofNat1728_ord_eq_zero_of_crossingPresentation), and is the $j = 1728$ counterpart of the corresponding statement centred at $j = 0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_NodeLocalized_exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_ofNat1728_width_dvd.lean

